# Senzing configuration update for the OFAC advanced mapper: TAX_ID_TYPE, for OLDER engine configs only.
#
# Apply with:  sz_configtool -f src/ofac_config_updates_tax_id_type.gtc
#
# Do NOT apply it to a config that already has TAX_ID_TYPE (Senzing 4.4's default config does, e.g. 4.4.3):
# sz_configtool reports each command as already present and does not save. Apply src/ofac_config_updates.gtc
# (the custom features) in either case.
#
# Adds TAX_ID_TYPE so tax identifiers can be typed on the TAX_ID feature (the mapper emits TAX_ID_TYPE=VAT / CUIT /
# INN; a generic tax number carries no type), mirroring the ID_TYPE element/attribute that NATIONAL_ID already
# has. Without it, TAX_ID_TYPE is dropped at load and distinct tax schemes collide in the single untyped
# TAX_ID namespace.
#
# These commands are for engines whose config predates TAX_ID_TYPE (e.g. 4.4.0-26224, whose template has
# NATIONAL_ID ID_TYPE scored but nothing on TAX_ID).
#
# Three steps mirror NATIONAL_ID: (1) bind the ID_TYPE element to the TAX_ID feature (stores/displays),
# (2) add ID_TYPE to the TAX_ID comparison call -- this is what makes the type actually SCORED, not just
# stored, (3) map the TAX_ID_TYPE attribute. execOrder values match the 4.4.0-26224 template. `save`
# persists the change.

addElementToFeature       {"feature": "TAX_ID", "element": "ID_TYPE", "derived": "No", "display": 1, "execOrder": 7}
addComparisonCallElement  {"feature": "TAX_ID", "element": "ID_TYPE", "execOrder": 3}
addAttribute              {"attribute": "TAX_ID_TYPE", "class": "IDENTIFIER", "feature": "TAX_ID", "element": "ID_TYPE", "required": "Desired"}
save
